    {
      "id": "claim_f37d02c968d94079a20e443d772a740c",
      "statement": "The PostgreSQL helper executes each query on its stored cursor and commits after successful execution, returns the current cursor result through `fetch_all()`, and closes its cursor and connection through `close()`; it does not catch driver exceptions or provide an explicit rollback path.",
